WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.120
Move over, Lannisters – a "House of the Dragon"&nbsp;
scene is taking us back to the ickiest days of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.440
"Game of Thrones." Warning: spoilers ahead&nbsp;
for "House of the Dragon" episode four.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.600
If that scene in the depths of King's&nbsp;
Landing’s underworld grossed you out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.960
you're not alone — but the actors involved&nbsp;
were apparently just fine with it.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.720
In the fourth episode of this brand new&nbsp;
hit "Game of Thrones" spin-off from HBO,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:25.280
Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen — played in her&nbsp;
youth by Milly Alcock — ends up exploring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.631
the underbelly of King's Landing&nbsp;
with her troublemaking uncle Daemon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.631 --> 00:00:32.080
who takes her beyond the walls of the Red&nbsp;
Keep for a stealthy night on the town.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.000
After taking in a crude show about&nbsp;
the Targaryen line of succession&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.680
(which paints Rhaenyra in a pretty&nbsp;
unflattering light) and several drinks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:44.240
the two abscond to a brothel together,&nbsp;
which... gets pretty weird pretty quickly.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.080
Daemon escorts his niece through the crowded&nbsp;
establishment, taking in scenes of people in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:53.440
various compromising positions, before assuming&nbsp;
one himself: a passionate kiss with his own niece.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.680
Rhaenyra responds, however, and the two&nbsp;
really start to go at it before Daemon demurs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.160
apparently in part due to "performance issues,"&nbsp;
which he's dealt with in previous episodes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.360
This scene may have been pretty&nbsp;
uncomfortable to watch on multiple levels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:08.720
but according to Alcock, it was&nbsp;
kind of a breeze to actually film.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.560
Speaking to The New York Post, Alcock said&nbsp;
the scene was surprisingly routine to shoot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:17.120
thanks to coordinators behind the scenes as well&nbsp;
as her solid off-screen relationship with Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.880
an industry veteran who's appeared in&nbsp;
everything from "Doctor Who" to "Morbius."

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.560
As Alcock told the Post,

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.720
"[Smith and I] were just kind of mates. So, it was&nbsp;
quite comfortable. We had an intimacy coordinator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:30.480
and we worked with her through the rehearsal&nbsp;
process and blocked it out months before."

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.680
That said, there was one major surprise:&nbsp;
the brothel itself. Alcock continued,

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.520
"Clare Kilner, our director, made sure that&nbsp;
we hadn't seen any of the brothel stuff until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:43.200
we were shooting. So, that was our first time&nbsp;
walking through the brothel, and he's guiding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.120
her through the room with all of these other&nbsp;
bodies. So, that was quite shocking. You're like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:52.080
'This is kind of weird and silly.' There were&nbsp;
extras who we had just met who were like, 69-ing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:57.760
for 12 hours. It's pretty gnarly. We felt pretty&nbsp;
overdressed, because everyone else was nude."

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:02.080
"Directing scenes like that can be really&nbsp;
difficult. It's a big responsibility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:06.623
and it's important to shoot it&nbsp;
from the right point of view."

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:10.960
Clearly, Alcock and Smith were put as at&nbsp;
ease as possible during this tricky scene...&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.560
even with the inherent weirdness of their&nbsp;
surroundings during this pivotal moment.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:18.720
As the predecessor to "House of the Dragon,"&nbsp;
HBO's juggernaut "Game of Thrones" drew plenty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:23.520
of controversy due to its often brutal depictions&nbsp;
of sexual violence against women — and it seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.120
that "House of the Dragon" may be taking a&nbsp;
different approach, particularly in Episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.920
4. When Rhaenyra is left high and dry after her&nbsp;
encounter with Daemon, she returns home only to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:37.360
seduce Ser Criston Cole, taking complete control&nbsp;
in the encounter and savoring every minute of it.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:41.520
"House of the Dragon" also shows the other side of&nbsp;
the coin in this episode with Alicent Hightower,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.480
the second wife and queen to Rhaenyra's father&nbsp;
King Viserys. Expected to be available any time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:50.560
the king requests, Alicent is awoken in the&nbsp;
middle of the night for one of his visits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:54.960
and is depicted as emotionless and vacant during&nbsp;
the act itself; though it's not a violent scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:59.520
it's an unsettling portrayal of what it looks&nbsp;
like to, as a woman in a medieval era, forego&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:04.400
your personal boundaries and pleasure as part of&nbsp;
a patriarchal structure like an absolute monarchy.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.280
In any case, it does seem like the&nbsp;
actors on set for "House of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.590
Dragon" are well-protected behind the scenes,&nbsp;
no matter how controversial those scenes are.

